  <<V:c1_slow5:mean>>, <<V:c1_slow5:tok>>. So for about the same cost to decode the new tenant trains about 1.8 times
  as much; and with the usual tenant the p99 of decode's single-step time is still <<V:c1_slow5:s99>> above the
  no-tenant value, with the new tenant <<V:cvfm_slow5_step:s99>>.
- **Target 15 %**: with the new tenant (pause after the step) decode's mean is <<V:cvfm_slow15_step:mean>> slower and
  the tenant progresses at <<V:cvfm_slow15_step:tok>> tokens per second. The usual tenant on the same night:
  <<V:c1_slow15:mean>>, <<V:c1_slow15:tok>>. So decode slows less and the tenant trains about 1.5 times as much; the
  p99 of single steps is <<V:cvfm_slow15_step:s99>> against <<V:c1_slow15:s99>>.
- **The two rows of the usual tenant are one run each, and where the automatic setting settles differs from run to
